# IT Asset Tracker

A full-stack web app for tracking company IT equipment such as laptops, phones and routers. You can see who has each device and what state it's in.

## Features

- Add, edit and delete assets
- Assign each asset to a person
- Track status: In use, In repair or Retired
- Search by name, type or assigned person
- Filter by status
- Data stored in a SQLite database, so it persists between restarts

## Tech stack

| Layer     | Technology              |
| --------- | ----------------------- |
| Front end | React (Vite), CSS       |
| Back end  | Node.js, Express        |
| Database  | SQLite (better-sqlite3) |

## Screenshot

![IT Asset Tracker](screenshots/app.png)

## Getting started

You need Node.js 20 or newer.

```bash
git clone https://github.com/Ankrah3/it-asset-tracker.git
cd it-asset-tracker
```

**Start the API (terminal 1)**

```bash
cd server
npm install
npm run dev
```

The API runs at `http://localhost:5000`. The database file is created automatically on first run.

**Start the front end (terminal 2)**

```bash
cd client
npm install
npm run dev
```

Open the address Vite prints, usually `http://localhost:5173`.

## API

| Method | Endpoint          | Description                                  |
| ------ | ----------------- | -------------------------------------------- |
| GET    | `/api/assets`     | List all assets (optional `?status=` filter) |
| POST   | `/api/assets`     | Create an asset                              |
| PUT    | `/api/assets/:id` | Update an asset                              |
| DELETE | `/api/assets/:id` | Delete an asset                              |

## Project structure

```
it-asset-tracker/
├── client/    React front end
├── server/    Express API and SQLite database
└── README.md
```

